# Friendai — local environment template.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` at the repository root and edit the values you need.
# `.env` is git-ignored and local to your checkout; this template is committed.
# A variable set in your shell wins over the same key in `.env`.
#
# Format: one `KEY=value` per line. Blank lines and lines starting with `#` are ignored,
# surrounding double or single quotes are stripped, and a leading `export ` is accepted.

# ─── Variables the build reads from `.env` ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Where the built mod jar is dropped for manual testing.
#
# `./gradlew deployTestJar` — and every `./gradlew assemble` / `build`, which runs it as a
# finalizer — deletes older `friendai-*.jar` (and `friendai-*.jar.sha256`) files from this
# directory and copies the freshly built `friendai-<version>.jar` into it. Other mods and files
# in the directory are never touched, and the directory is created when it is missing. If the
# jar cannot be deleted because the game is still running, the task fails with that message.
#
# Accepted values:
#   - an absolute path, Windows or POSIX style: `C:/Users/you/.../mods`, `C:\Users\you\...\mods`
#     or `/home/you/.minecraft/mods` (forward slashes are safest on every platform);
#   - a path relative to the repository root, for a folder inside the checkout;
#   - unset, empty or commented out: the task skips and nothing outside the repository is
#     written. This is the default in a fresh checkout.
#
# Typical values: the `mods` folder of the Minecraft instance you test in, for example
#   official launcher:   C:/Users/<you>/AppData/Roaming/.minecraft/mods
#   Modrinth App:        C:/Users/<you>/AppData/Roaming/ModrinthApp/profiles/<instance>/mods
#   PrismLauncher:       C:/Users/<you>/AppData/Roaming/PrismLauncher/instances/<instance>/mods
#   dedicated server:    C:/servers/minecraft/mods
#   a local staging dir: /test-builds-drop
TEST_BUILD_PATH="C:/Users/you/AppData/Roaming/ModrinthApp/profiles/My Instance/mods"

# ─── Variables this file does NOT set ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# These are read by Gradle or the build's host process before `.env` is ever opened, so they
# belong in your shell, IDE run configuration or wrapper invocation, not here.

# JAVA_HOME — a JDK 25. Gradle and Loom refuse older JVMs, so every command needs it when your
# default `java` is older:
#   JAVA_HOME="C:/Program Files/Eclipse Adoptium/jdk-25.0.4.101-hotspot" ./gradlew build
#
# GRADLE_OPTS — extra JVM options for the Gradle client. CI uses a non-daemon build:
#   GRADLE_OPTS="-Dorg.gradle.daemon=false"

# Build knobs that exist only as `-D` system properties (see AGENTS.md, "Commands"):
#   ./gradlew test -Dfriendai.golden.write=true            rewrite the engine prompt goldens
#   ./gradlew test -Dfriendai.tts.voice=<voice dir>        opt into the gated local-TTS spike
#   ./gradlew test -Dfriendai.live=true -Dfriendai.live.config=<server config path>
#                                                          opt into the live provider evaluation
#   ./gradlew runGameTest -Dfabric-api.gametest.filter='friendai-gametest:<class>_tests_*'
#                                                          run one GameTest class
